      "writtenOn": "2018-07-19T09:01:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This particular change is because we are now including rt tasks in schedtune groups, so I thought we needed a way to include their boost in the resulting total.\n\nIf we don\u0027t change this function what happens is that we will enable the boost group when an rt-task is available, but the boosted utilisation percentage will be based upon the utilisation reported by cfs. The overall outcome of that might be fine - with the proportional boost used in schedtune, a 50% boost gives you 50% of the remaining util so if the cfs util is low, we\u0027d apply a large boost, but it feels like that would make it hard to reason about the boost settings which should be applied.\n\nThe choice I made here was to aggregate the reported rt and cfs utilisation, and then apply the boost, which is likely to result in lower boost application but should be consistent.\n\nPatrick made a different choice in his utilclamp set on mainline, he boosts both signals independently and then uses max(boosted_rt, boosted_cfs, cfs+rt).\n\nI think it\u0027s a matter of interpretation what we actually do here, all options result in boost being applied, but I\u0027m trying to get to an implementation where the result is predictable. I think Patrick\u0027s version might be more intuitive than this one, so I\u0027d happily change this. Using something closer to utilclamp also has the benefit that any change in functionality is a bit easier to understand when we eventually switch over in future android kernels.\n\nAre you happy with the way it is now Phil or would you like to change it?",
      "parentUuid": "8e87f92f_871e0332",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6290,
        "startChar": 41,
